<https://vocab.eona-x.eu/alignments/map-charging-mode> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-06-26"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
	<http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "EONA-X Vocabulary Hub — EV-charging crosswalk (EMDS demo, #446)" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "relatedMatch (associative, not equivalence): DATEX II chargingMode (IEC 61851 modes 1-4, encoding AC/DC plus control) and NeTEx currentType (AC/DC) both characterise how charging is delivered, but at different granularity, so related rather than close or exact." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/netex/currentType> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#relatedMatch> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/datex-ii/chargingMode> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Charging mode ↔ current type"@en ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/alignments/netex-datex-ii> ;
	a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> , <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> .
<https://vocab.eona-x.eu/alignments/map-voltage> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-06-26"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
	<http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "EONA-X Vocabulary Hub — EV-charging crosswalk (EMDS demo, #446)" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "closeMatch: DATEX II 'voltage' and NeTEx 'nominal voltage' both denote the operating voltage of the charging equipment in volts (V); near-equivalent, framing differs slightly." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/netex/nominalVoltage> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/datex-ii/voltage> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Voltage ↔ nominal voltage"@en ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/alignments/netex-datex-ii> ;
	a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> , <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> .
<https://vocab.eona-x.eu/alignments/map-max-power> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-06-26"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
	<http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "EONA-X Vocabulary Hub — EV-charging crosswalk (EMDS demo, #446)" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "closeMatch: both denote the maximum power the equipment can deliver, but DATEX II expresses it in kilowatts (kW) and NeTEx in watts (W); same quantity, different unit framing, so close rather than exact." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/netex/maximumChargingPower> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/datex-ii/maxPowerAtSocket> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Maximum power at socket ↔ maximum charging power"@en ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/alignments/netex-datex-ii> ;
	a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> , <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> .
<https://vocab.eona-x.eu/alignments/map-station> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-06-26"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
	<http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "EONA-X Vocabulary Hub — EV-charging crosswalk (EMDS demo, #446)" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "closeMatch: DATEX II EnergyInfrastructureStation and NeTEx RechargingStation both denote the place that groups the charging points/equipment of a site; near-equivalent groupings, not asserted strictly identical." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/netex/RechargingStation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/datex-ii/EnergyInfrastructureStation> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Station ↔ recharging station"@en ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/alignments/netex-datex-ii> ;
	a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> , <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> .
<https://vocab.eona-x.eu/alignments/map-location> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-06-22"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
	<http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "EONA-X Vocabulary Hub — EV-charging crosswalk (EMDS demo, #446)" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "exactMatch: both denote the geographic location of the charging facility (latitude/longitude resp. Transmodel Point/Location); the same real-world concept, interchangeable." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/netex/location> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/datex-ii/location> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Location ↔ location"@en ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/alignments/netex-datex-ii> ;
	a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> , <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> .
<https://vocab.eona-x.eu/alignments/map-connector> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-06-22"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
	<http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "EONA-X Vocabulary Hub — EV-charging crosswalk (EMDS demo, #446)" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "closeMatch: DATEX II frames the connector as a 'type' and NeTEx as a 'standard'; the underlying enumerations (Type 2, CCS, CHAdeMO, ...) overlap heavily but the framings/value sets are not asserted identical, so close rather than exact. The individual code values are aligned one-by-one in the connector code-value block (exact/closeMatch); Tesla and generic domestic plugs have no 1:1 NeTEx counterpart and are left unmapped." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/netex/connectorStandard> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/datex-ii/connectorType> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Connector type ↔ connector standard"@en ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/alignments/netex-datex-ii> ;
	a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> , <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> .
<https://vocab.eona-x.eu/alignments/map-power> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-06-22"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
	<http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "EONA-X Vocabulary Hub — EV-charging crosswalk (EMDS demo, #446)" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "exactMatch: both denote the rated electrical power of the charging facility in kilowatts (kW); same quantity and units, interchangeable." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/netex/powerRating> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/datex-ii/power> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Rated power ↔ power rating"@en ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/alignments/netex-datex-ii> ;
	a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> , <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> .
<https://vocab.eona-x.eu/alignments/map-status> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-06-22"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
	<http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "EONA-X Vocabulary Hub — EV-charging crosswalk (EMDS demo, #446)" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "closeMatch: both denote the operational availability status of the charging facility; DATEX II's status enumeration and NeTEx's availabilityStatus are not guaranteed value-for-value identical, so close rather than exact." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/netex/availabilityStatus> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/datex-ii/status> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Status ↔ availability status"@en ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/alignments/netex-datex-ii> ;
	a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> , <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> .
<https://vocab.eona-x.eu/alignments/map-charging-point> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-06-22"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
	<http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "EONA-X Vocabulary Hub — EV-charging crosswalk (EMDS demo, #446)" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "closeMatch, not exactMatch: DATEX II models the single charging *point* whereas NeTEx models the charging *equipment* (the physical unit, which may expose several points); the concepts overlap closely but are not strictly equivalent." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/netex/ElectricVehicleChargingEquipment> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/datex-ii/ElectricVehicleChargingPoint> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Charging point ↔ charging equipment"@en ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://vocab.eona-x.eu/alignments/netex-datex-ii> ;
	a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> , <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> .
